NNAAMMEE
     ggiiff — generic tunnel interface

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     ppsseeuuddoo--ddeevviiccee ggiiff

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ggiiff interface is a generic tunnelling pseudo-device.  It can tunnel
     IPv4, IPv6, and MPLS over IPv4 and IPv6, with behavior mainly based on
     RFC 4213 IPv6-over-IPv4.

     A ggiiff interface can be created at runtime using the iiffccoonnffiigg ggiiff_N ccrreeaattee
     command or by setting up a hostname.if(5) configuration file for
     netstart(8).

     The ggiiff interface must be configured with the addresses used for the
     outer header.  This can be done by using ifconfig(8)'s ttuunnnneell command
     (which uses the SIOCSLIFPHYADDR ioctl).

     The addresses of the inner header must be configured by using ifconfig(8)
     in the normal way.  The routing table can be used to direct packets to‐
     ward the ggiiff interface.

